  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: 110. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '110 (One Hundred and Ten) is an Irish trick-taking game with bidding, related to Twenty-Five. Played with a standard 52-card deck; the first player or team to reach 110 points wins. Players score 5 points per trick. Card ranking varies by trump suit.',
    objective: 'Be the first player (or team) to reach 110 points. Each trick is worth 5 points; the holder of the highest trump in play gets an extra 5 points.',
    gameplay: "Bidding (10, 15, 20, 25, or 60) starts left of dealer; dealer may 'take' by equalling the bid. Highest bidder picks up the five-card kitty, discards five, and names trump (no robbing). Player to dealer's left leads; same card ranking as Twenty-Five (5 of trump highest, then J, then A of hearts).",
    keyRules: [
      'Bids: 10, 15, 20, 25, 60; dealer can take by equalling',
      'Bidder takes kitty, discards 5, names trump',
      '5 points per trick; +5 for highest trump in play',
      'First to 110 wins',
    ],
